From bbe72bd52325fb0e70f1fc71caf19ed5f845d498 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nova <361320585+q2-nova@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:29:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] irqchip and clocksource: add X2000 per-core interrupt and
 OST support

Use the Q2 vendor kernel register layout: 0x100 per-core stride for INTC
and OST, a global 64-bit counter, and core-local timer interrupts on IP4.
Configure per-CPU IRQ descriptors before requesting per-CPU IRQs.
Validated with two CPUs, clocksource selection and userspace timer tests
in the Q2 emulator; this is not hardware validation.
